ake your solution more faster, it you will precalculate some small primes. Also you can use "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"map"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" < "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"int"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"int"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" >  to store calculated values. DP base "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"d"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"]["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"] = "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"curBeauty"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" — is a current beauty of the array."}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Second. Greedy. Let's find position "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"r"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", which can upgrade our answer. If there some values of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"r"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" — we will take most right position. We will add this position to the answer and upgrade our answer. Why it's correct? Let's fix an optimal solution (sequence of position, where we used an upgrading operation) "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"r"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" > "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"r"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"2"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" > ... > "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"r"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":". Also we have an solution which was built by using greedy "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"l"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1"}],"kind